// Watchlist size over time, by BDC and by parent manager: $ at risk (USD M) and
// position count per tier, on BOTH a fair-value and an amortized-cost basis,
// plus the corresponding % of total book. Powers the by-manager view. From the
// first quarter whose chances are calibrated to realised formation: before it
// the tiers would be the model's raw chances, another basis. In reporting season
// a late filer's newest quarter carries the tiers the watchlist publishes (its
// book centred on the newest level) until it files, and a manager's row adds up
// its BDCs' rows. A sum across BDCs (an industry figure) reads the by-BDC
// *_history fields instead: the same tiers on each quarter's own calibration,
// equal to the published ones except on that late filer's newest quarter.
//
// Prefer the *_cost / pct_book_cost fields for severity SHARES: an FV basis
// shrinks the numerator and the denominator with the same markdown that put the
// loan on the list, damping the signal. Use the fv_* fields for "$ at risk",
// where marking to market is the point.
//
